      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substituting \\(S=8\\) and \\(R=16\\) gives \\(16=8g-4,\\) so \\(g=\\tfrac52.\\) Hence, when \\(S=10,\\) \\[ R=\\frac52(10)-4=21. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "First substitute the given values of \\(R\\) and \\(S\\) to determine \\(g\\)",
        "The first pair gives \\(16=8g-4\\)"
